/// \file mutmultiarray.mla
/// \brief Mutable fixed-size multidimensional arrays (std::mutmultiarray).
///
/// `mutmultiarray<T, D1, ..., DN>` has the same fixed shape as `multiarray`,
/// but permits indexed and compound writes when declared with `var`.
///
/// ```mlang
/// mod std::mutmultiarray;
///
/// var matrix: mutmultiarray<i32, 2, 2> = {{1, 2}, {3, 4}};
/// matrix[0][1] = 42;
/// matrix[1][0] += 10;
/// ```
///
/// Constant invalid `[]` indexes are compile-time errors. Dynamic `[]`
/// accesses abort at runtime when out of bounds. For recoverable access,
/// `get(i1, ..., iN)` returns `option<T>`:
///
/// ```mlang
/// var row: i32 = 1;
/// let value: i32 = matrix.get(row, 0).unwrap();
/// let missing: bool = matrix.get(2, 0).is_none();
/// ```
///
/// `is_some()` and `is_none()` inspect the result without panicking.
/// `unwrap()` returns the element or reports its source location and aborts if
/// the result is `None`. The number of `get` indexes must match the number of
/// dimensions. A `let` binding remains immutable.

// @builtin mutmultiarray
// Mutable fixed-size multidimensional array:
// mutmultiarray<T, D1, ..., DN>.
// This module is a documentation/navigation anchor for
// `mod std::mutmultiarray;`.

